      "problem": "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14116975/assets/f3118303ab755b84d1a8065e3fef0ff13c2ff44e3601c3aae0207022b64c09fa.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14116975/assets/dd226e3cb1952497d8f546e4ee73d4860f23ccda89662bc2a4012f583aa6dc24.svg) Find $\\dfrac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a}+\\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ and each component of $\\mathbf{b}$ by $\\dfrac{1}{2}.$ Then, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}a+\\frac{1}{2}b & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1-2 \\\\ 2-3 \\\\ 4+1 \\\\ -3-4 \\\\ 1+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
